  "question": {
    "text": "At what temperature a gold ring of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>230</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> be heated so that it can be fitted on a wooden bangle of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>241</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>? Both the diameters have been measured at room temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.<br />(Given: coefficient of linear thermal expansion of gold <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
