  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>To fit gold ring of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>230</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> over wooden bangle of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>241</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, gold ring expansion is required.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>241</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>230</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>241</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>230</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>152</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p>",
